.TH OSK 4
.SH NAME
osk \- the keyboard on the screen's files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /mnt/osk/ctl
.br
.B /mnt/osk/status
.br
.B /mnt/osk/words
.br
.B /mnt/osk/keys
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IR Wm-osk (1)
serves these files at
.B /mnt/osk
(Lucifer mounts them there for every application it starts).
.TF status
.TP
.B ctl
Requests, one a write:
.RS
.TF "\fBrecord \fIfile\fR|\fBoff"
.TP
.B show
a text field has the keyboard: show it, unless a keyboard of the
machine's is attached
.TP
.B hide
none has: hide it
.TP
.B toggle
hide it to its handle, or show it
.TP
.BI layout " name"
the letters' layout
.I name
(a file in
.BR /lib/osk/layouts ),
kept for next time
.TP
.BR mode " text" | plain
what the field holds: prose, whose words are put right and whose
sentences begin with a capital, or not (a shell's commands, code), whose
words are only offered
.TP
.BR correct " on" | off
.TP
.BR swipe " on" | off
whether words are put right, and strokes read as words
.TP
.BI height " pixels"
the keys' height (0: from the screen's size)
.TP
.BI record " file" \fR|\fPoff
record the touches and what is typed in
.I file
.RI ( wm-osk (1)'s
.BR -r ),
or stop
.TP
.BI learn " word ..."
the words, as words of the typist's
.TP
.BI rect " x y w h"
.TP
.B ontop
accepted, and not needed: where a text field is, for a keyboard the
view must be moved above
.RI ( softkbd (2));
this one is docked, the field above it already
.PD
.RE
.TP
.B status
What it is showing, a line each:
.BR state " shown" | handle | hidden ,
.BI layout " name" \fR,
.BR mode ,
.BR correct ,
.BR swipe ,
.BI height " pixels" \fR,
.BI keyboards " n"
(1 when a keyboard of the machine's is taken to be attached),
.BI words " n"
(the words in the list, 0 until it is read) and
.BR shift " none" | once | locked .  The first
read of an open file answers at once; each later read waits until the
status changes.
.TP
.B words
The words learned,
.I "word count"
a line; a write of such lines adds them.
.TP
.B keys
The keys shown and where they are, a line each:
.IP
.I "name minx miny maxx maxy"
.IP
in screen pixels,
.I name
the character a key types, or the key's word in the layout
.RB ( shift ,
.BR space ,
.BR del ,
.BR enter ,
.BR sym ,
\&...).  Empty while the keys are not shown.  For a test, an agent, or a
trace's reader, to find a key.
.PD
.SH EXAMPLE
Switch to Dvorak and wait for the keyboard to change:
.IP
.EX
echo layout dvorak > /mnt/osk/ctl
read 400 < /mnt/osk/status
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/osk.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR wm-osk (1),
.IR softkbd (2),
.IR cons (3)
